  "answers": [
    "The summary doesn't give a clean answer, because the data for those three days is incomplete.\n\n- **Oct 1:** There are no records, so the day is missing.\n- **Oct 2:** The day shows 0 steps. That's probably the day the watch was off.\n- **Oct 3:** 6,000 steps.\n\nThe tool reported an average of 3,000 steps a day. That figure counts Oct 2 as a real 0 and averages it with Oct 3. The same summary also says it excluded one day as no-wear, so its output contradicts itself. I wouldn't trust the 3,000.\n\nIf Oct 2 was a no-wear day, the only day with usable data is Oct 3, so your average is **6,000 steps**, from one day. That's the figure I'd go with.\n\nYou may have left the watch off on Oct 1 or Oct 2, and the data fits either one. Oct 1 is missing entirely, and Oct 2 has a zero-step day. If you want, I can sync your latest data to see whether Oct 1 fills in."
  ],
